use ../../../lib/UiComponent

export ui-component Switch:
    description:
        A switch turns a setting on or off, like a light switch. Flipping it
        takes effect straight away, with no Save or OK step.

    states:
        On or off, with nothing in between. Flipping it switches the state and
        tells the component using it. That component can also set the state at
        any time, such as switching it back if the change couldn't be applied.

    name:
        The name says what the setting is, such as "Wi-Fi", and stays the same
        whether it's on or off. Whether it's on is conveyed separately.

    activation:
        The user flips it the usual way for the platform: clicking, tapping,
        dragging the knob, or using the keyboard. Clicking its label also flips
        it. Which keys do this is up to the chosen library.

    disabled:
        A disabled switch can't be flipped, and it's clear to the user that it's
        unavailable. It keeps showing whether it's on or off.

    nonGoals:
        - No partly-on state. That's a Checkbox
        - Not for choices saved later with the rest of a form. That's a
            Checkbox
